`SparseTable` stores values under non-empty string keys. `put(key, value)` must deep-copy the value into storage and permit any value, including `None`. `fetch(key)` must return a deep copy of the stored value and raise `KeyError` only when the key is absent. `contains(key)` reports presence, and `snapshot()` returns a deep copy in insertion order. All key-taking methods raise `TypeError` for non-string keys and `ValueError` for empty keys. Updating an existing key must not change its position. No returned or supplied mutable value may alias internal state.

